x86_64-linux  One clang-only name, `__cxa_free_exception`: the cleanup clang lays down for a throw whose *object's own constructor* throws, freeing the storage `__cxa_allocate_exception` handed back before the object was ever in flight. cxx1 has no cleanup around the construction of a thrown object and so never calls it - the same difference throw-out-of-handler.nonames records, and nothing this case does reaches it. Every other name agrees, `__cxa_end_catch` and the destructors this case is about included.
arm64-darwin  The same one name with Mach-O's leading underscore, `___cxa_free_exception`, for the same reason. Every other name agrees.
